# render needs a chart kind; with needs parentheses.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | render | render chart with title = 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..46
  PIPELINE@0..45
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    RENDER_OP@9..15
      IDENT@9..15 "render"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
    PIPE@16..17 "|"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    RENDER_OP@18..35
      IDENT@18..24 "render"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      IDENT@25..30 "chart"
      WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
      RENDER_PROPS@31..35
        IDENT@31..35 "with"
    WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
    ERROR@36..45
      IDENT@36..41 "title"
      WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
      EQ@42..43 "="
      WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
      LONG@44..45 "1"
  WHITESPACE@45..46 "\n"

error[DS0120]: `render` must be the last operator
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | from t | render | render chart with title = 1
  |          ^^^^^^   ----------------- this operator comes after `render`
  |          |
  |          the chart is drawn at this point
  |
  = help: a query draws one chart: keep only the last `render`

error[DS0101]: expected a chart kind after `render`, found `|`
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | from t | render | render chart with title = 1
  |                 ^
  |
  = note: the chart kinds are `table`, `timechart`, `linechart`, `areachart`, `barchart`, `columnchart`, `piechart`, `scatterchart` and `card`

error[DS0101]: expected `(` after `with`, found `title`
  --> query:1:37
  |
1 | from t | render | render chart with title = 1
  |                                     ^^^^^
